# Rust / Cargo
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock

# Build artifacts
*.pdb
*.exe
*.lib
*.dll
*.exp
*.o
*.obj
*.a

# Test output files
nova_test_output.h264
test.h264

# Runtime-generated / sensitive — never commit
nova_cert.der
nova_cert.pem
nova_key.der
# Echo/relay peer identities — Identity::load_or_create writes
# <prefix>.cert.der / <prefix>.key.der into its data dir, which is the CWD by
# default. Running echo-client or nova-relay from the repo root would otherwise
# drop a private key into the working tree.
*.cert.der
*.key.der
nova_cert.version
nova_paired.txt
nova_paired.json
nova_debug.log
nova.log
nova-service.log
nova-input.log
vigem_install_declined.flag
nova.toml

# IDE / Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Android
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/
echo-data/
relay-data/

# Local recordings and bug-report bundles.
#
# Both are written beside the executable, so in a normal build they land under
# the already-ignored /target/. Named here anyway because of WHAT they contain:
# a recording is a capture of somebody's desktop and a report bundle carries a
# desktop screenshot plus redacted logs. A stray one committed from a manual
# run is not a build artifact, it is a disclosure.
recordings/
bugreports/

# Xbox / UWP client
#
# `bridge/` holds the staged Rust DLL + import lib — build output, reproduced by
# xbox\build-bridge.ps1. `packages/` is the C++/WinRT NuGet restore. "Generated
# Files" is the C++/WinRT projection, regenerated on every build and large.
xbox/EchoXbox/bridge/
xbox/packages/
xbox/EchoXbox/Generated Files/
xbox/EchoXbox/x64/
xbox/EchoXbox/Debug/
xbox/EchoXbox/Release/
xbox/.vs/
AppPackages/
BundleArtifacts/
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.appxupload
# The package signing key. A temporary VS-generated one is still a private key,
# and a committed one signs anything anybody builds from this tree.
*.pfx
xbox/EchoXbox/*.cer
# MSBuild's intermediate dir for this project is EchoXbox\EchoXbox\<plat>\<cfg>\
# (IntDir defaults to $(ProjectName)\...), which the x64/ rule above does not
# reach. Ignore the whole nested build tree.
xbox/EchoXbox/EchoXbox/

# The sideload bundle build-app.ps1 produces: a copy of the .msix, the signing
# certificate and a redistributable framework package, zipped. Every byte of it
# is reproducible from a build, and it is ~3 MB per run.
xbox/dist/
